# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE, a nonidentity correspondence through the copy: the root's a3, declared `@: Model a3 c`,
# holds c, a merge of Cand {pad; x; x}; User's paths through the free input a3 read the coordinates of Model {x}.  In
# u1, a copy of User, the ordinal `[0]x` reads Cand's first x (slot 1, 1) and the bare `x` -- the LAST occurrence --
# its last x (9): neither is Model's own place.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Model:
    int: x 0
end: Model
Cand:
    int: pad 5
    int: x 1
    int: x 9
end: Cand
User:
    int: y 0
    int: z 0
    y: a3\[0]x
    z: a3\x
end: User
u1: merge: User
c: merge: Cand
@: Model a3 c
u1
int: ok 7
if: u1\y != 1 || u1\z != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
